      "role": "labelled_checkpoint",
      "reached_rerank": true,
      "status": "completed",
      "displayed_text": "On identifying two people at the same site with the same suspected infection onset within 48 hours, declare an outbreak immediately: the registered manager declares the outbreak and notifies the local Health Protection Team the same day, begin enhanced cleaning in affected areas using the product/frequency advised by the Health Protection Team or the site infection lead, cohort affected people (and where practicable staff) away from unaffected people, restrict or reshape communal activities per the Visiting Arrangements Policy exception, and monitor and log staff and residents' symptoms daily for the duration of the outbreak.\n\nRecord-keeping: retain a daily case log tracking new cases against the incubation period and a brief dated decision log of every significant outbreak decision (for example when enhanced cleaning began, when cohorting was applied or relaxed), since the registered manager must keep these records to show the process was followed and to support later review or regulatory enquiry.",
